// crossroads.js — the prompts for Rare Air (cave.html). Every junction in the
// cave is one of these.
//
// Each prompt lists the answers the game recognises, sorted into tiers by how
// often people give them. The tiers are hand-estimated, not counted — there is
// no server behind this page — so treat them as a well-informed guess that
// live answer counts can correct later (see rarityOf in cave.js).
//
// common     the handful of answers most people reach for first
// clever     an "unusual" answer so many people pick on purpose that it isn't
//            unusual any more
// uncommon   known to everyone, said by few
// rare       valid answers most people wouldn't think of
// deep       the obscure end of the list
// uncharted  one hidden answer per prompt; finding it opens a chamber
//
// Answers are separated by "|"; "/" separates spellings of the same answer
// (the first is the one shown). Case, accents, punctuation, spaces, a leading
// "the" and plurals are ignored when matching, so "Brussels sprouts" finds
// "brussels sprout". Every prompt should be answerable from a finite list —
// anything not listed is a dead end, so lists err on the side of generous.

